Subject: [PATCH 4/4] app: no tips about new features in the editor
From: Office Kit
Date: 2026-10-19
Upstream: https://github.com/BRF-Tech/filex-office-editor (AGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 2026 BRF Tech)
Base: v0.3.1 57dda3dae99af78eb26b3c64b69f1e3f711f0757 (the tag commit; the next main commit acc87f88da47 changes only README.md)
Apply: git -C <filex checkout> apply <this file>   (in order: 0001, 0002, 0003, 0004)
Modified: this patch changes filex-office-editor; see docs/office-editor-patches.md (Office Kit)

Office Kit: 편집기의 '신규' 기능 풍선(새 버튼 안내)을 끈다 (customization.features.featuresTips = false).

The editor shows a tip balloon about each new feature ("New button:
Format") the first time it is opened. In the sandboxed editor frame it
cannot remember that the tip was closed, so it comes back every time,
and it covers the toolbar. ONLYOFFICE's own setting
customization.features.featuresTips = false turns the tips off.

 src/app/config.ts        | 5 ++++-
 tests/app-config.test.ts | 1 +
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/app/config.ts b/src/app/config.ts
index 1a000c2..ebc46aa 100644
--- a/src/app/config.ts
+++ b/src/app/config.ts
@@ -349,7 +349,10 @@ export function editorConfig(o: ConfigInput): Record<string, unknown> {
         plugins: false,
         macros: false,
         mentionShare: false,
-        features: { spellcheck: { mode: false, change: false } },
+        // No tips about new features: they name buttons of the full editor
+        // and come back every time (the sandboxed editor cannot remember
+        // that they were closed).
+        features: { spellcheck: { mode: false, change: false }, featuresTips: false },
         ...(phone ? phoneLayout() : o.narrow ? narrowLayout() : {}),
       },
     },
diff --git a/tests/app-config.test.ts b/tests/app-config.test.ts
index 7b331d6..3596f27 100644
--- a/tests/app-config.test.ts
+++ b/tests/app-config.test.ts
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ describe('the editor configuration', () => {
     expect(c.editorConfig.user).toEqual({ id: EDITOR_USER_ID, name: 'Ayşe' });
     expect(c.editorConfig.customization).toMatchObject({ forcesave: true, plugins: false, macros: false, help: false, feedback: false, goback: false, uiTheme: THEME_LIGHT });
     expect(c.editorConfig.customization.features.spellcheck).toEqual({ mode: false, change: false });
+    expect(c.editorConfig.customization.features.featuresTips).toBe(false);
     expect(c.document.permissions).toMatchObject({ edit: true, download: false, print: false, chat: false });
     expect(c.editorConfig.customization.chat).toBeUndefined();
     // "Suggest a feature" opens ONLYOFFICE's site, which the sandbox cannot.
